    {
      "id": "612fc65a145b4cdd",
      "role": "C",
      "mission": {
        "base_commit": "cfb4a739deeb9a904c4a878935de7fcbfd6198ac",
        "delegation_parent": "R/C",
        "depth": 1,
        "epoch": 1,
        "hypothesis": "A balanced contiguous OpenMP partition of the flattened point set, combined with per-thread max-heaps and a deterministic merge, should remove shared updates and improve the scan cost from O(P*k) insertion work to O(P log k). It may help most when the point set and k are large enough to offset heap, sorting, and merge overhead.",
        "id": "612fc65a145b4cdd",
        "ordinal": 1,
        "parent_id": null,
        "role": "C",
        "source_commits": [],
        "sources": [],
        "transformations": {
          "files": [
            "src/knn.c"
          ],
          "retained": [
            "Build group prefix offsets and statically divide the flattened points into balanced contiguous ranges across the OpenMP team.",
            "Give each thread a private max-heap capped at min(k, its assigned point count), avoiding locks and retaining only its locally best candidates.",
            "Order candidates by squared distance and encounter index, sort each private candidate list, then merge the lists deterministically before applying the existing label sort and vote behavior.",
            "Preserve the baseline -1 label padding when fewer than k points are available and keep all per-call state local."
          ]
        },
        "tree_id": "e1:C",
        "trial_id": "01M542PFK4XH263Q0Y5BCF6EPJ",
