        "depth": 1,
        "epoch": 1,
        "hypothesis": "Storing each group in contiguous x and y coordinate planes should make the point scan more cache-friendly than interleaved Point records. A bounded max-heap keeps candidate storage O(k) and uses encounter order to preserve stable distance-tie selection.",
        "id": "4e5248ae712349b9",
        "ordinal": 2,
        "parent_id": null,
        "role": "A",
        "source_commits": [],
        "sources": [],
        "transformations": {
          "files": [
            "src/knn.c",
            "src/knn.h"
          ],
          "retained": [
            "Changed each group's point storage from interleaved Point records to x/y structure-of-arrays planes in one allocation, filled during parsing.",
            "Scanned the coordinate planes sequentially and hoisted query coordinates out of the point loop.",
            "Used a max-heap ordered by squared distance and original encounter index, then retained the existing label sort and vote logic."
          ]
        },
